BAVER Unit: CAD Specification & Internal Construction Guide
1.0 Unit Overview
Core Specifications
Designation: BAVER-45 (Blast-Activated Viscous Elastic Retardant - 45kg)

Form Factor: Spherical with ogive (tapered) nose section

Diameter: 400 mm (15.7 inches)

Height: 420 mm (with nose)

Total Mass: 45.0 kg (99.2 lbs)

Payload Mass: 30.0 kg (66.1 lbs) - Gel components

Structural/Dispersal Mass: 15.0 kg (33.1 lbs)

Density: ~0.75 g/cm³ (will float if water entry occurs)

2.0 Materials Specification
2.1 Shell Components
Component	Material	Thickness	Purpose	Environmental Note
Main Body	Molded cellulose pulp + PLA binder composite	8 mm	Biodegradable, impact resistant	Decomposes in 3-6 months in soil
Internal Liner	Food-grade silicone coating	0.5 mm	Moisture barrier, chemical inert	Non-toxic, prevents component interaction
Nose Cone	PLA with bamboo fiber reinforcement	6 mm	Aerodynamic stability	Higher strength for impact zone
Fins (4x)	PLA with flax fiber	4 mm	Stabilization during descent	Biodegradable composite
2.2 Internal Components
Component	Material	Specification	Purpose
Central Dispersal Charge	PETN (Pentaerythritol tetranitrate)	75 grams, molded disk	Low-yield explosive for dispersion
Membranes (6x)	Seaweed-based alginate film	0.2 mm thickness	Ruptures at 50 psi to mix components
Internal Baffles	Cornstarch-based bioplastic	2 mm, honeycomb structure	Component separation pre-detonation
Fuze Housing	PEEK (Polyether ether ketone)	Machined, IP67 rated	High-temp, waterproof electronics housing


3.0 Internal Construction - CAD Assembly Guide
3.1 Section View (Cutaway) Description
From center outward:

text
1. CENTRAL CORE (30mm diameter)
   ├── MEMS Fuze Assembly
   │   ├── IMU (Inertial Measurement Unit)
   │   ├── Barometric altimeter
   │   ├── Safe/Arm mechanism
   │   └── RF shielding cage
   ├── PETN Dispersal Charge (75g, disk-shaped)
   └── Detonator leads (energized at 20m AGL)

2. LIQUID CHAMBER (Radial Sections - "Orange Wedges")
   ├── 6 sealed compartments (each 5.0kg capacity)
   ├── Contains: Water + Fluorine-free Class A foam + preservative
   ├── Lined with alginate rupture membranes
   └── Pressurized to 30 psi with nitrogen for rapid expansion

3. DRY POWDER MATRIX (Between liquid wedges)
   ├── Calcium polyphosphate (40% - 12.0kg total)
   ├── Carboxymethyl cellulose hydrogel powder (15% - 4.5kg)
   ├── Fumed silica thixotropic agent (5% - 1.5kg)
   └── Pre-mixed, free-flowing powder

4. SHELL & STRUCTURAL ELEMENTS
   ├── Molded pulp/PLA composite shell (8mm)
   ├── Food-grade silicone inner liner (0.5mm)
   ├── External groove pattern for aerodynamic spin
   └── 4 biodegradable PLA/flax fins (120° apart)
3.2 Key CAD Features to Model
1. Biodegradable Shell Pattern:

text
External surface should show:
- Hexagonal dimple pattern (10mm across flats) for:
  a) Aerodynamic boundary layer control
  b) Controlled fracture points during dispersal
  c) Increased surface area for biodegradation
- Four fin slots (90° spacing)
- Mating flange for nose cone (threaded PLA insert)
2. Internal "Orange Wedge" Baffle System:

text
Model six radial compartments:
- Each wedge: 60° arc, extending from 50mm radius to 190mm radius
- Separated by cornstarch bioplastic baffles (2mm thick)
- Each contains spherical bulge (for liquid expansion) and flat rupture membrane facing center
3. Nose Cone Assembly:

text
- Ogive shape: 100mm height, 0.5 caliber radius
- Contains:
  * Radar altimeter antenna window (clear PLA section)
  * GPS patch antenna (if included for tracking)
  * Frangible impact cap (breaks away on ground contact)
- Threads onto main body (M300x4 thread, 30mm engagement)
4. Fin Design:

text
- 4 fins, 60mm height, 80mm root chord, 40mm tip chord
- 5° cant angle for induced spin (200-400 RPM in descent)
- Snap-fit attachment to shell grooves
- Made from PLA with 20% flax fiber for stiffness
